So my first ascension was a human wizard, which took about 3 years to
achieve, and now I've been making much faster progress with human
archaeologists, having had one who even made it to Gehennom. I've had
at least 5 runs that could easily have ended in ascension, thanks to
early wands of wishing and other such goodies, but each time I run
into a new YASD that none of my hundred or so wizards ever succumbed
to.

The latest was on DLVL10, where I had donated for some protection from
a priest and then proceeded to kill the priest to get my money
back...except, he/she somehow managed to paralyze me before I could
deal the mortal blow with Grayswandir. I died; the priest did not.
Now, I've killed dozens of priests before with no problem, and I came
to believe that they are little more than pushovers to a well-prepared
character. The good news is that I left a bones pile with a BoH full
of loot, including a wand of wishing (4 uses left!) and the bulk of an
ascension kit.

But how is it that a priest can paralyze an unsuspecting adventurer,
and why has this not happened to me before? Also, when I encounter the
bones level I died on, will the priest still be angry? I know
shopkeepers carry grudges from game to game.


